Package: fluorine-desktop
Architecture: all
Depends: hyprland, hypridle, hyprlock, waybar, kitty, fuzzel,
 sway-notification-center, swaybg, grim, slurp, wl-clipboard, cliphist,
 brightnessctl, wireplumber, jq, libnotify-bin, network-manager, bluez,
 blueman, power-profiles-daemon, kanshi, wdisplays, pulsemixer, pavucontrol,
 btrfs-progs, snapper, podman, distrobox,
 thunar, thunar-volman, thunar-archive-plugin, tumbler, gvfs, gvfs-backends,
 file-roller, unzip, zip, xz-utils, swayimg, zathura, zathura-pdf-poppler,
 mousepad, galculator, btop, xdg-user-dirs,
 python3, python3-gi, gir1.2-gtk-4.0, gir1.2-adw-1
Recommends: fluorine-artwork
Description: FluorineOS AMOLED Hyprland desktop environment
 FluorineOS desktop configuration for Hyprland 0.55 and later, built on a
 pure AMOLED black base with a reactive lime accent.
 .
 The package installs the native Lua compositor configuration, Waybar,
 Kitty, Fuzzel, and SwayNotificationCenter themes, the hypridle idle policy
 and hyprlock lock screen, hardware media and brightness key bindings,
 cliphist clipboard history, and the flr-shot, flr-keys, flr-doctor, and
 flr-onboard command line utilities.
 .
 Hardware integration covers NetworkManager connections through nmtui, the
 Bluetooth manager, power profile cycling through power-profiles-daemon, and
 automatic external display layouts through kanshi.
 .
 flr-ctl provides a single keyboard-driven system menu in Fuzzel for network,
 Bluetooth, display, audio, power, diagnostics, and session actions, and
 flr-update refreshes APT metadata, lists incoming FluorineOS and security
 upgrades, and reports whether a reboot is required. On a Btrfs root it
 creates a pre-update snapshot before applying the upgrade.
 .
 flr-snapshot creates, lists, and rolls back Btrfs snapshots through snapper,
 refreshing the GRUB menu when a snapshot generator is installed.
 .
 flr-mode switches between work, focus, and present workstation profiles and
 reports the active profile in the Waybar badge. flr-box creates development
 containers with rootless Podman and Distrobox so toolchains stay off the host
 APT database.
 .
 flr-shader cycles the display between color-accurate, warm low-blue-light, and
 grayscale shaders through the Hyprland screen_shader decoration option, and
 restores the saved choice on the next login.
 .
 flr-wall switches the desktop wallpaper from the shipped 4K set or from
 ~/Pictures/Wallpapers, remembers the choice across logins, and keeps the
 hyprlock lock screen background in step with it.
 .
 flr-settings is a native GTK4 and libadwaita control panel with a two-pane
 navigation layout. It covers wallpapers, the display shader, window gaps and
 border width, the workstation profile, the idle lock timeout, the first-login
 cheat sheet, live monitor state and scale, network and Bluetooth status with
 direct launchers, power profiles, default sink and source volume, and the
 OS, memory, ZRAM, and Btrfs snapshot summary. Every control delegates to the
 matching flr-* command, so the panel and the keyboard workflow share one
 state. flr-config owns the editable state in ~/.config/fluorine/config.lua
 and applies it to Hyprland and hypridle.
 .
 The daily-driver utilities follow the same palette: Thunar with volume and
 archive plugins plus Tumbler thumbnails, File Roller for zip, tar, and 7z
 archives, swayimg as the Wayland image viewer, Zathura with Poppler for
 recolored dark PDF viewing, Mousepad for plain text, and galculator as a
 floating calculator. Default MIME handlers in /etc/xdg/mimeapps.list and
 /etc/skel/.config/mimeapps.list route directories, images, documents, and
 archives to those applications, and xdg-user-dirs-update runs at session
 start so the standard home folders exist for the Thunar sidebar.
 .
 Configuration is installed into /etc/skel/.config so that newly created
 users receive the FluorineOS desktop on first login. The first interactive
 login shows the keybinding cheat sheet once.
